  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Amino acids are organic compounds that contain amine&nbsp; and carboxyl &nbsp;functional groups, as well as a side chain specific to each amino acid. There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> standard amino acids that are used to create proteins.</p><p>One letter codes of the given natural amino acids are<br />Natural amino acid&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; One Letter Code<br />(A) Glutamic acid&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(III) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math><br />(B) Glutamine&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(I) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math><br />(C) Tyrosine&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;(IV) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math><br />(D) Tryptophan&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(II) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Correct match is<br />(A)-III, B-I, (C)-IV, (D)-II</p></blockquote>"
